  "description": "# LSC-02 | Fun 002 | Sync Luma Guest to SF Campaign\n\n**📋 Ticket:** [Luma guests → Salesforce campaign members](https://brightdata-group.monday.com/boards/8667788707/pulses/13343839880)\n\n---\n\n**TRIGGER:** Called by LSC-02 | Main | Hourly Luma Guests → SF Campaign Members\n\n**PURPOSE:** Add a Luma guest to the Salesforce campaign mapped to the Luma event, with the Luma approval status.\n\n**FLOW:**\n1. Normalize email, map status (approved → Registered = Approved, pending_approval → Registered = Pending)\n2. Search Contact and Lead by email → Salesforce (Contact wins when both exist)\n3. Find SF campaign ID by Luma slug → Google Sheet; get Campaign name → Salesforce\n4. Search CampaignMember → update Status or create\n\n**DB / TABLES:** Google Sheet `1rShm0qyQFdtqf8b6FEpR6F3pFOEvrdWtdrklsX3axGw` / Sheet1 (`Luma event slug` → `SF campaign ID`)\n**UPSTREAM:** LSC-02 | Main | Hourly Luma Guests → SF Campaign Members  \n**DOWNSTREAM:** none\n\n## Important logic\n- Returns `Skipped` when: invalid email or unsupported Luma status.\n- Returns `Not found` when no Contact/Lead exists yet (message also notes a campaign issue).\n- Returns `Campaign not found` when Contact/Lead exists but the slug is not in the sheet, the ID is invalid, or the campaign doesn't exist in SF.\n- Campaign must have member statuses **Registered = Approved** and **Registered = Pending**.\n- Email and IDs are validated in Ruby before being placed in SOQL.\n",
  "name": "LSC-02 | Fun 002 | Sync Luma Guest to SF Campaign",
